FidelityFX API headers from AMD's FidelityFX SDK v2.4.0
(github.com/GPUOpen-LibrariesAndSDKs/FidelityFX-SDK), MIT as each file says,
for frame generation (host/framegen.cpp) and, on Linux, FSR 3 upscaling
(host/upscaler_ffx.cpp): ffx_api.h, ffx_api_types.h, ffx_upscale.h,
ffx_framegeneration.h, ffx_framegeneration_api_types.h, vk/ffx_api_vk.h and
vk/ffx_api_framegeneration_vk.h, with their #include paths made relative to
this folder, and ffx_api.h's FFX_API_ENTRY (__declspec(dllexport)) defined
only on Windows - empty elsewhere, where bbhost calls the FidelityFX API
through pointers it looks up, never the declarations. The Windows runtime -
amd_fidelityfx_loader_vk.dll, amd_fidelityfx_upscaler_vk.dll and
amd_fidelityfx_framegeneration_vk.dll, AMD-signed - is not here: it goes
beside bbhost.exe, as the upscaler bridge's (tools/fetch_upscalers.sh).

LICENSE-signedbin.md is the SDK's own licence document
(Kits/FidelityFX/docs/license.md), which names the files under its MIT terms.

For Linux, bbhost builds its own FidelityFX library, libbbhost_fidelityfx_vk.so,
from the SDK's source (src/ffx_vk, CMakeLists.txt BBHOST_FFX):
  - source.sha256: the SDK files the build takes, each pinned by SHA-256 at the
    same tag (tools/fetch_fidelityfx.sh fetches them; none is in this
    repository), every one on the licence's MIT list;
  - patches/: the changes made to them, each saying why, under the same MIT
    terms (applied by tools/fetch_fidelityfx.sh).
